    "updated_at": "2017-09-18T14:43:40Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the prompt response, Anne, and sorry I'm slow getting back to you. I'll try to stay more on top of this.\r\nThe requirement in the first of our two use cases is to control subscribed notifications that come from outside the current application. The idea is to generalize a mobile device's \"Do Not Disturb\" functionality across all browsing/application environments, desktop as well as mobile.\r\nThe second use case could certainly be handled by the application, but we think it would be far easier to allow the AT a user is relying on to get this on/off effect using the same gesture, regardless the underlying application.\r\nDoes this help explain things? I think we're actually far more concerned with the first use case as people working on payments in W3C believe its applicability is wider than just accessibility. However, we believe both use cases present accessibility requirements.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
